# AI Executive Intelligence Platform

## Engineering philosophy

This repository implements the AI-Powered Executive Intelligence Platform.

The authoritative design documents are located in /docs.

## Rules

- Build incrementally.
- Do not implement future architecture unless required by the current milestone.
- Prefer simple solutions over premature distributed architecture.
- Keep deterministic logic deterministic.
- LLM outputs must be validated with Pydantic.
- LLM providers must be abstracted from domain logic.
- Agents should not directly access databases.
- Business logic must be independently testable.
- Mock LLM calls in unit tests.
- Do not assert exact LLM prose in tests.
- Add integration tests at system boundaries.
- Use Python type hints everywhere.
- Use TypeScript strict mode.
- Never commit secrets.
- Explain significant architectural choices before implementing them.
- Do not add a dependency without explaining why it is needed.
- Run tests and linting after every meaningful change.
- Keep PR-sized changes small.
- Do not refactor unrelated code.
- Follow the existing repository architecture rather than inventing new patterns.

## Architecture direction

Eventual stack:
- Next.js 16
- FastAPI
- Google ADK
- LiteLLM
- FastMCP
- PostgreSQL
- Pinecone
- Celery
- Redis
- Langfuse
- Sentry
- Pydantic

This is the eventual architecture, NOT a requirement to introduce every component immediately.

## Current priority

Build one working vertical slice before expanding scope:

RSS → Trend Agent → Quality Gate → Persistence → API → Dashboard.
